component SigilProjectionStore {
  goal {
    Publish *disposable source-bound assertions* without accepting stale or
    *out-of-order reconstruction* as current.
  }

  interface {
    DisposableCleanup {
      Clean only *generated worlds* while holding the same exclusive *writer lock*.
      Recover even from a *malformed index* without interpreting its contents. Remove
      symlink artifacts themselves without following their targets. Keep the
      *lock inode* in place so cleanup cannot split *concurrent writers*. Preserve
      *authored sources*, workspace configuration and *external preparation inputs*.
    }

    ImplementationCommands {
      Prepare exactly one copied source file, *fixed ontology* and
      *identity-only catalog* for the *external semanticizer*. Keep its binding with
      the caller. Require *current non-Disjoint Design* and validate all catalog
      references before ingesting Implementation. Accept an
      *explicit source selection* for stale inspection and comparison. Compile each
      world independently, then compare *Design obligations* with
      *Implementation closure* in the *fixed matcher*. Completed *Closed* is green
      and *Converged* is yellow with warnings; both exit zero. *Drift* is red and
      exits one. Apply this mapping to compile implementation and compare. Missing
      current Design catalog leaves comparison unavailable, exits three, and never
      reports Drift.
    }

    CurrentImplementation {
      Select *arbitrary-language source files* and assemble only
      *fresh indexed assertions* against the *current frozen Design catalog*.
      Validate *resource identity* again on reading and enforce
      *aggregate assertion limits* before closure. Keep the catalog out of
      *Implementation evidence*. Saturate in an independent *EGraph* and identify the
      *captured selection*, catalog and assertion contents. Missing sources and
      completed empty facts remain distinct. Explicit empty selection is visible in
      the report.
    }

    DesignCommands {
      Expose prepare, ingest, stale and compile for Design and entities for its
      catalog. Accept an explicit *frontend bundle* and workspace root. Preparation
      writes only bound Design context, fixed ontology and a *semantic binding* into
      a new *caller-selected directory*. Refuse to overwrite existing directories.
      Ingestion checks the binding source and current inputs before publication.
      Compile Design exits zero for *Coherent* (green) or *Loose* (yellow with
      warnings), and one only for *Disjoint* (red). Invalid options exit two;
      *operational failure* without a completed *semantic result* exits three.
      Inspection exits are command-specific: stale returns one for nonfresh sources,
      and entities returns one when no current catalog is available. Neither
      inspection exit is a semantic color. No provider, model or
      *automatic repair options* exist.
    }

    CurrentDesign {
      Assemble *fresh source projections* against a recaptured *frontend snapshot*.
      Add only structural type and label facts plus required *unit inventory* from
      the frontend. Missing projections leave Design Loose unless fresh facts already
      establish Disjoint. Frontend errors produce no completed verdict. Validate the
      complete identity set before freezing a current catalog. Reports identify
      captured inputs, projection contents and *compiled eqval*. Prepare Design
      context only from its bound source and *dependency closure*.
    }

    ProjectionPublication {
      Capture the expected *per-source generation* before reconstruction. Under one
      OS file lock, compare the *prepared binding* and generation with current inputs
      and recheck source and *Design dependency bytes*. Publish bounded
      *data-only assertions* by temporary-file replacement, then atomically replace
      the index that binds their checksum to inputs and generation. Reject duplicate
      preparations and changed source, catalog or format inputs. *Publication tokens*
      cannot repeat after cache deletion and reconstruction; an old binding cannot
      regain authority when disposable generations restart. Keep scheduling and
      workers outside the store.
    }

    BindingHistory {
      Retain accepted projections for distinct semantic bindings of the same source
      in the *disposable world store*. Keep one current source-path publication and
      address superseded projections by their complete *binding fingerprint*,
      including the Implementation Design-catalog identity. Reuse a retained
      projection only when its complete binding is fresh for the current operation.
      Do not key this cache by worker or scope identity, and do not turn it into an
      *external-work ledger*.
    }

    IndexedAssembly {
      Mirror *normalized source paths* with their original extensions plus egg. Load
      only *index-selected assertions* with matching complete input bindings and
      checksums. Parse them as *restricted data*. Missing, stale, corrupt, deleted
      and unindexed objects contribute no *current facts*. Bound index and assertion
      bytes separately. Refuse *path traversal*, *symlinked artifact paths* and
      malformed index metadata. A *busy writer lock* is an operational failure, never
      a semantic result.
    }
  }
}
